<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Not found — Clawdia' }) %>
    <%#
        Deliberately no Open Graph tags and no member-specific text. This is the
        one answer every failed gate gives — a guild whose public page is off, a
        member who has not opted in, a member who is not here at all — so it must
        describe none of them, or the 404 itself would confirm which case it is.
    -%>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#faf6ef">
    <style>
        body { background: var(--cream-50); color: var(--ink-950); }
        .cwp-empty { max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px; text-align: center; }
        .cwp-empty h1 { font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif; font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
        .cwp-empty p { color: var(--ink-500); font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 28px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main class="cwp-empty">
        <h1>Nothing here</h1>
        <p>This page is private, does not exist, or has not been turned on. Public server pages are opt-in.</p>
        <a href="/" class="cw-btn cw-btn-dark">← Back to Clawdia</a>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
